From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bernardo Pereira <bpereira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Detect blocks inside inline shadow hosts through the flat
 tree

A block descendant breaks its inline ancestors out of the inline
formatting context. is_or_contains_block walked the light-DOM children,
so it missed blocks in a shadow tree or assigned to a slot, and an inline
host around them shrink-wrapped instead of filling its container.

Walk the flat tree. (Upstream already looks through display: contents.)
---
 src/node/node.rs | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/node/node.rs b/src/node/node.rs
index 2098425..8fafce0 100644
--- a/src/node/node.rs
+++ b/src/node/node.rs
@@ -615,7 +615,8 @@ impl Node {
     }

     fn any_child_is_or_contains_block(&self) -> bool {
-        self.children
+        // Flat tree: an inline shadow host's blocks live in its shadow root.
+        self.flat_children()
             .iter()
             .any(|&child_id| self.tree()[child_id].is_or_contains_block())
     }
